Upgrade procedure for sqlite3

Source:	https://sqlite.org/YEAR/sqlite-autoconf-XYYZZPP.tar.gz
	(3.54.1 is sqlite-autoconf-3540100.tar.gz)
Checksum: sqlite.org publishes a SHA3-256 hash for each download on
	https://sqlite.org/download.html and for sqlite3.c on
	https://sqlite.org/changes.html; there is no signature.

Vendor branch:	vendor/sqlite3/dist
Vendor tag:	vendor/sqlite3/dist/VERSION
In-tree prefix:	contrib/sqlite3
Last imported:	3.54.1

To upgrade to a new version:

1. Download the autoconf tarball into an empty directory, check its
   SHA3-256, and extract it with --no-same-owner.
2. Use the vendor-update skill (vendor/sqlite3/dist, contrib/sqlite3).
   Copy everything except tea/, keeping MIDNIGHTBSD-Xlist and
   MIDNIGHTBSD-upgrade on the vendor branch.
3. Subtree merge into master.  Makefile.msc, Replace.cs and
   sqlite3.rc are deleted on master; keep them deleted.
4. Update Version: in sqlite3.pc.
5. Check the release notes (https://sqlite.org/changes.html) for
   removed or renamed compile-time options and grep sqlite3.c for each
   option in lib/libsqlite3/Makefile.
6. Build lib/libsqlite3, usr.bin/sqlite3 and the consumers (lib/libmport,
   usr.sbin/mport, usr.sbin/aged, lib/libmsearch, usr.bin/msearch,
   usr.bin/kyua), then add an UPDATING entry.

MidnightBSD differences from FreeBSD:

  - libsqlite3 is a public library (libsqlite3.so.1, headers in
    /usr/include, sqlite3.pc in /usr/libdata/pkgconfig), not FreeBSD's
    PRIVATELIB, because mport and other base and third-party software
    link against it.
  - lib/libsqlite3/Makefile enables RTREE, FTS3, FTS4, FTS5, JSON1 (a
    no-op since 3.38), GEOPOLY, MATH_FUNCTIONS, SESSION, PREUPDATE_HOOK
    and COLUMN_METADATA, and links with -lz -lm -lpthread.  New options
    may be added; do not remove any.
  - usr.bin/sqlite3 builds the CLI from shell.c without readline.

Local patches applied on top of upstream:

  - sqlite3.pc: generated from sqlite3.pc.in with the values above.
